# Global project rules

## General principles

- **Always respond in English** - all comments, documentation, and communication should be in English.
- **Strict typing** - use strict typing everywhere possible. Avoid `any`, use `unknown` when necessary.
- **Explicit access modifiers** - always specify access modifiers (`private`, `protected`, `public`). Do not use implicit modifiers.
- **Readonly for injected services** - all constructor dependencies must be marked `readonly`.
- **Comments in English** - all code comments should be in English and explain "why", not "what".

## Formatting

- **Indent**: 2 spaces for all files
- **Quotes**: single quotes for TypeScript/JavaScript
- **End of file**: always add a blank line at the end of the file
- **Whitespace**: remove trailing whitespace

## File structure

- One class/interface/type per file
- File name must match the exported class/interface name (kebab-case)
- Use `index.ts` for re-exports from directories
